claim.claim-text:
announcing, by a proxy device, an availability of a trusted device;
in response to the announced availability, receiving, by the proxy device, a first request from a target device; and
upon receiving the first request from the target device, sending, by the proxy device, a second request to the trusted device, wherein the second request comprises a request for the trusted device to announce its availability directly to the target device from which the first request was received, and the trusted device establishes a communication connection with the target device based on the second request.

scanning, by a target device, for availability of a trusted device;
based on the scan, identifying a particular trusted device;
sending, by the target device, a first request for the particular trusted device to a proxy device that sends a second request to the particular trusted device;
receiving, by the target device and directly from the particular trusted device, another availability of the particular trusted device; and
establishing, by the target device, a communication connection directly with the particular trusted device responsive to receipt of the other availability.

receiving input to initiate a change in security state at the target device;
using the communication connection to perform a set of ranging operations to allow the target device to receive a set of authentication information; and
using the set of authentication information to change the security state at the target device.
